                            "relativePublishTimeDescription":  "7 months ago",
                            "rating":  4,
                            "text":  {
                                         "text":  "I really like this place for their family friendly seating and great menu options. The food is just ok though, and a lot of the quality of things like bread, salad, and sides are clearly very cheap + bland but designed to make it feel like you got a very deluxe set meal.\nTheir pasta dishes and baked rice dishes are best by far of anything on the menu. The service is weird too. They have bizarre rules about seating when arriving between meal seatings (e.g. between breakfast and lunch) and will force guests to wait at the entrance instead of helping them to a seat even when the whole place it\u0027s completely empty. They clearly don\u0027t prioritize customer comfort or service in this way, and it\u0027s rather confusing.",
                                         "languageCode":  "en"
                                     },
