                            "relativePublishTimeDescription":  "3 months ago",
                            "rating":  5,
                            "text":  {
                                         "text":  "We almost missed Joyful Restaurant because the entrance is literally inside a phone case shop beside Xin Fu Tang. Walk in, go upstairs, and suddenly there’s a full pasta place.\n\nNow I understand why Taipei has so many pasta spots. It’s not the super traditional Italian style, but honestly it works. The pasta is al dente and the flavors are very Asian-friendly.\n\nWe ordered the carbonara and the spicy seafood pasta and both were really good, but the spicy seafood was the winner for me. So flavorful with just the right kick — the kind of dish that makes you want to come back again.\n\nSkip the burgers and drinks o👀",
                                         "languageCode":  "en"
                                     },
