                            "rating":  4,
                            "text":  {
                                         "text":  "A fine dining restaurant that needs reservations in advance and deposits.\n\nThe food is Chinese Taiwanese with fusion feel. They don’t serve wine so you need to get your own and there will be a cleaning fee for each glass used or per bottle basis.\n\nThe deco is very interesting as it retains the old tradition Taiwanese houses and structures with modern settings.\n\nThe food was all fine and beautifully presented. Everything tasted good, especially the Chicken Soup, very satisfying. The fruits and vinegar drinks were more ordinary.\n\nThey were quite strict about the dining time limits of 2 hours, so you need to be prepared and be mindful about it.\n\nYou can bring your own wine and they will provide glasses but not serve you., which means you need to do it yourselves.",
                                         "languageCode":  "en"
                                     },
