                            "relativePublishTimeDescription":  "6 months ago",
                            "rating":  5,
                            "text":  {
                                         "text":  "Red Hot Chili Peppers would be proud of this place. Plus they\u0027d go well with pizza 😉\nRustic, punk and rock n roll vibes inside the quaint but cool atmosphere. Two kind individuals showed me where to enter this rather unique space. I googled best pizza options in Taipei, and this location came up. One look at the building, you could believe it\u0027s in NYC, but nope. Only a short  walk from Huashan 1914 Creative Park, you\u0027ll be able to salvage your appetite. I needed a small but good bite so I got myself the Small Clone - a signature slice. A very good, credible crust (fold), savory taste, and cooked to the right golden colour of crisp. I devoured the slice for obvious reason. As you can see, the dab of oil resembles a bear 🐻 I\u0027m a happy bear. Great job UTB!",
                                         "languageCode":  "en"
                                     },
