                            "text":  {
                                         "text":  "I think the most noteworthy aspect of this café is its interior design. The furniture, from the dining tables to the shelves and chairs, gave off a European vibe. The café itself offers a relaxing atmosphere with a quaint, French small-town feel. I visited on a weekday afternoon, so it was not too crowded, but I imagine it gets busy on weekends. It\u0027s a good idea to make a reservation before you visit. The brunch plate is decent—while not particularly impressive, it is above average compared to other cafés in Taipei.",
                                         "languageCode":  "en"
                                     },
