                            "rating":  4,
                            "text":  {
                                         "text":  "I was going to give this review a 5 stars but having to pay $34 for tea in the end was a bit disappointing.  Tea was served without asking so I presumed it’s complementary. It’s good tea so I don’t mind paying, just wish I’ve been told. The egg fried rice was one of the best i ever had and the pork cutlet was largely good, a few bit felt a little dry.  The soup was good too, but not the flavour that I’m used to, maybe it’s a regional style, i won’t mark it down cos it’s not what I’m used to.  Dining environment was good too.  Air con was very powerful but the food stayed mostly hot right till the end.",
                                         "languageCode":  "en"
                                     },
