                            "name":  "places/ChIJny7cm_mrQjQRXc1MKexwNQA/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT20xRmRWazBYMlpxWmxwNWEybHRWMjVhTW1VNFNuYxAB",
                            "relativePublishTimeDescription":  "10 months ago",
                            "rating":  5,
                            "text":  {
                                         "text":  "Went there with my family for a Taiwanese Hokkien singer performance and some light bites.\n\nI really liked their handmade bean curd rolls, which were filled with chives, coriander, and shrimp.\n\nWe also had the sous vide duck breast, turnip cake with salted egg yolk, and braised pork ears.\n\nThe duck breast was a bit dry and the texture was too firm. The turnip cake was good, while the pork ears were a bit too oily and salty.\n\nWe also ordered some drinks. As for cocktails, I’d say they were mediocre. I’d recommend going for hard liquor or beer instead.\n\nThe vibe was great, and the service was excellent.",
                                         "languageCode":  "en"
                                     },
                            "originalText":  {
                                                 "text":  "Went there with my family for a Taiwanese Hokkien singer performance and some light bites.\n\nI really liked their handmade bean curd rolls, which were filled with chives, coriander, and shrimp.\n\nWe also had the sous vide duck breast, turnip cake with salted egg yolk, and braised pork ears.\n\nThe duck breast was a bit dry and the texture was too firm. The turnip cake was good, while the pork ears were a bit too oily and salty.\n\nWe also ordered some drinks. As for cocktails, I’d say they were mediocre. I’d recommend going for hard liquor or beer instead.\n\nThe vibe was great, and the service was excellent.",
                                                 "languageCode":  "en"
                                             },
