                            "relativePublishTimeDescription":  "6 months ago",
                            "rating":  4,
                            "text":  {
                                         "text":  "We finally made it to this famous xiao long bao spot, and it was absolutely packed with customers! Despite the major crowd, the auntie working there was super helpful and managed to get us seated quickly, which we really appreciated. However, the food itself was a bit hit-or-miss for us. We tried both the crab meat and the pork xiao long bao.\n\nHonestly, we found the overall flavor profile a bit lacking. The biggest disappointment was the crab meat xiao long bao; the filling had a strange, slightly sand-like texture that wasn\u0027t pleasant. The standard pork xiao long bao were just okay. Ultimately, while the service was fantastic, we concluded that perhaps the flavor here is a bit too local for our personal taste preferences.",
                                         "languageCode":  "en"
                                     },
                            "originalText":  {
                                                 "text":  "We finally made it to this famous xiao long bao spot, and it was absolutely packed with customers! Despite the major crowd, the auntie working there was super helpful and managed to get us seated quickly, which we really appreciated. However, the food itself was a bit hit-or-miss for us. We tried both the crab meat and the pork xiao long bao.\n\nHonestly, we found the overall flavor profile a bit lacking. The biggest disappointment was the crab meat xiao long bao; the filling had a strange, slightly sand-like texture that wasn\u0027t pleasant. The standard pork xiao long bao were just okay. Ultimately, while the service was fantastic, we concluded that perhaps the flavor here is a bit too local for our personal taste preferences.",
                                                 "languageCode":  "en"
                                             },
